<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="70543" href="schedule/2021/spring/CSE/498/70543.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2021" href="schedule/2021.xml">2021</calendarYear><term id="120211" href="schedule/2021/spring.xml">Spring 2021</term><subject id="CSE" href="schedule/2021/spring/CSE.xml">Computational Science and Engineering</subject><course id="498" href="schedule/2021/spring/CSE/498.xml">Special Topics</course></parents><sectionNumber>DM </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Intro to Digital Materials</sectionTitle><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Meets with ME 598 (48380) and MSE 598 (70522).  We introduce the connection of materials and data science, and specific issues regarding experimental and computational materials data. Topics include data acquisition and management, data curation, uncertainty quantification, and applying machine learning to materials data. The focus will be on current scientific literature in the emerging materials and data area.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Graduate - Urbana-Champaign.</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2021-01-25Z</startDate><endDate>2021-05-05Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="OLC">Online Lecture</type><start>11:00 AM</start><end>12:20 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><instructors><instructor lastName="Wagner" firstName="L">Wagner, L</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>